  "scientific_interpretation": "Under matched data, graph, width, depth, pooling, head, and optimization settings, Static PNA does not outperform Static GCN: validation MAE is higher for PNA in all three seed-matched comparisons, its across-seed mean MAE and RMSE are higher, and its mean R2, prediction-SD ratio, and calibration slope are lower. This is a controlled architecture benchmark, not a parameter-count-matched operator ablation. Static PNA has approximately 9.76 times as many trainable parameters, so no effect may be attributed to its aggregation mechanism alone. Because the substantially larger PNA did not establish a robust validation advantage, a parameter-capacity control is not scientifically required to support the conclusion that increased PNA complexity did not solve the static-model limitation.",
